+# DP83TC815 PTP / PSF Notes
+
+This note is a working reference for the DP83TC81x PSF-backed timestamp work in this tree.
+It is intentionally short and only keeps the details that matter for parser and matcher changes.
+
+## Key datasheet points
+
+- Source: `PHY datasheets/dp83tc815_Datasheet_text_only.txt`
+- Table 7-4 lists the timestamp-related registers:
+  - `PTP_TXCFG0` `0x0D12`
+  - `PTP_TXTS` `0x0D08`
+  - `PTP_RXTS` `0x0D09`
+  - `PTP_RXHASH` `0x0D2B`
+  - `PSF_CFG0..4` `0x0D14`, `0x0D21`, `0x0D22`, `0x0D23`, `0x0D24`
+
+## TX timestamp model
+
+- `PTP_TXTS` is only a timestamp queue.
+- The datasheet text says the host normally knows transmit order, so only the timestamp needs to be recorded.
+- Extra TX identity is optional.
+- `PTP_TXCFG0[14]` `TX TimeStamp Info Enable` enables latching:
+  - `messageType`
+  - `hash`
+  - `sequenceId`
+  - along with the TX timestamp, and transmitting those fields through PSF.
+
+Implication:
+
+- TX `seqId/msgType/hash` matching must be treated as a PSF-format feature gated by `PTP_TXCFG0[14]`.
+- Do not assume `PTP_TXTS` itself carries TX identity.
+
+## RX timestamp model
+
+- `PTP_RXTS` explicitly provides six 16-bit reads in this order:
+  1. `Timestamp_ns[15:0]`
+  2. `Overflow_cnt[1:0], Timestamp_ns[29:16]`
+  3. `Timestamp_sec[15:0]`
+  4. `Timestamp_sec[31:16]`
+  5. `sequenceId[15:0]`
+  6. `messageType[3:0], source_hash[11:0]`
+
+Implication:
+
+- RX identity tuple is architecturally real and not just an implementation detail.
+- If PSF is being used as the transport for RX timestamps, the parser should be aligned with:
+  - `sequenceId`
+  - `messageType`
+  - `source_hash`
+
+## Receive hash filter
+
+- `PTP_RXHASH[12]` enables filtering based on the ten-octet `sourcePortIdentity` hash.
+- `PTP_RXHASH[11:0]` programs the expected hash value.
+
+Implication:
+
+- The `hash` field is part of the intended receive identification model.
+- We currently parse it in the driver, but the live matcher does not yet use it.
+
+## Current implementation guidance
+
+- Keep CPTS as the authoritative live timestamp source until PHY matching is proven.
+- Treat PHY RX/TX lookups as shadow diagnostics.
+- When changing PSF parsing:
+  - check the parser against the register model above
+  - do not infer stronger guarantees than the datasheet gives for TX identity
+  - prefer comments that say whether a field is:
+    - guaranteed by `PTP_RXTS`
+    - optional via `PTP_TXCFG0[14]`
+    - still inferred from observed PSF layout
